Z||000000||GREENDANO||07-27-99||02:35 PM||||A while back somebody was looking for the fix to keep the temp gauge from pegging at start-up. <br>My buddy sent me the info. <br>Here's the link--&gt;http://www.tir.com/~jaski/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm<br>  It has lots of good pictures and has very detailed instructions as well.<br>   Dan-O
Z||000001||batboy||07-27-99||06:13 PM||||Thanks for sharing! I added that to my Fiero bookmarks.
Z||000002||theogre||07-27-99||08:05 PM||||He's got good pictures, but he goes a bit far,,,,, you don't need to remove the whole dash module, just the back. You can get to the ignition switch faster by loossening the 2 nuts, and left bolt, removing only the right bolt from the steering column slip braket. DO NOT remove bolts that hold the braket on the column! That lets you get the connector off the switch. The connector has 2(TWO) release ears that you must squeeze.<p>The repair can be done with NO cutting of the factory harness. The terminals for the ignition connector are common service repair items. You can also salvage them from defog, or trunk latch switch connectors, usually with some wire attached. Pop the new terminal into the ignition block and jump it to the correct wire in the dash. The connector is released by inserting a small screw driver into the switch face of the shell between the terminal and the out side face of the block. ((Can we tell how much Ogre hates cutting up factory wire? And how many times he's fixed other peoples cutting? :) )) 
Z||000003||GREENDANO||07-27-99||08:51 PM||||That's a good sugestion.  I haven't "fixed" my gauge yet because it isn't broken.<br>  I got my eye on you OGRE, sooner or later I'm gonna catch you cutting a factory wire.  HE HE.<br>  Dan-o
